            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="0610" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg478"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/2428: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Arica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Von
                            Tresckow</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-06-11T09:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 11, 1926—9
                                a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For Lassiter. Resolution which you have offered has aroused very bitter feeling
                    in Chilean Embassy here. They feel that it is unwarranted public indictment of
                    Chile and that honor will require her to break off negotiations and possibly to
                    break off relations with the United States. If Chilean Commissioner proposes any
                    possible solution or any compromise arrangement by which passage of resolution
                    would be avoided, please try to adjourn action and cable us immediately.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
